\f0\fs24 \cf0 # Diploid Genome Assembly QC & Annotation Pipeline\
\
A Snakemake workflow for evaluating and annotating a diploid (hap1/hap2)\
genome assembly. Runs a full suite of QC, structural validation, and\
annotation-transfer tools across both haplotypes in parallel, plus one\
combined whole-genome structural check.\
\
## What it does\
\
1. Preprocessing \'97 indexes each haplotype FASTA (minimap2 + samtools),\
   and builds a combined "diploid" reference for haplotype-aware analyses.\
\
2. Read aggregation & alignment \'97 concatenates HiFi and ONT read sets,\
   then aligns them both per-haplotype and to the combined diploid\
   reference.\
\
3. Structural error detection (Flagger) \'97 flags misassemblies,\
   collapsed regions, and duplications using both HiFi (diploid-combined)\
   and ONT (per-haplotype) read support, as two independent checks.\
\
4. Assembly QC \'97 standard completeness and contiguity metrics via BUSCO,\
   Compleasm, and QUAST, run per haplotype.\
\
5. Repeat masking \'97 soft-masks each haplotype using a custom repeat\
   library and outputs a repeat annotation BED file.\
\
6. Annotation transfer \'97 lifts over gene models from a reference genome\
   using Liftoff, extracts predicted proteins, and re-validates\
   completeness with protein-level BUSCO.\
\
7. Whole-genome alignment annotation (Cactus + TOGA) \'97 builds a\
   whole-genome alignment chain and uses it to transfer/evaluate\
   annotations, a more robust alternative to direct liftover for regions\
   with structural rearrangements.\
\
8. Segmental duplication detection (BISER) \'97 flags large, highly\
   identical duplicated regions in the assembly.\
\
## Requirements\
- Snakemake\
- Config file specifying: input FASTAs per haplotype, HiFi/ONT read\
  directories, reference genome/annotation paths, BUSCO/Compleasm\
  lineage databases, and tool container/script directories\
- Helper scripts (in scripts/) for Flagger, RepeatMasker, Compleasm,\
  Cactus/TOGA, and BISER steps\
- Conda, with the environment (NMR_T2T.yml) installed to run the current tools\
\
## Usage\
snakemake --configfile config.yaml --cores <N> [--cluster ...]\
\
